<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Dos Pilas</h1><p class="st-meta">629 CE – 810 CE (approx.) · capital Dos Pilas</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Maya kingdom founded in the Petexbatún region by a breakaway branch of Tikal's dynasty that sided with Calakmul and fought its own kin.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Dos Pilas was founded around 629 as an outpost of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tikal">Tikal</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bajlaj-chan-kawiil">B'ajlaj Chan K'awiil</a>, a member of the Tikal royal family, was installed there as its ruler, using the same emblem glyph. Defeated by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kaan">Kingdom of Kaan</a>, he became its ally and fought a long civil war against Tikal, defeating it in 679.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>His successors expanded the kingdom across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petexbatun">Petexbatún</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pasion-river">Pasión</a> region, conquering <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ceibal">Ceibal</a> in 735 and building hieroglyphic stairways recording their wars. Royal marriage linked the dynasty to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/naranjo">Naranjo</a> through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lady-six-sky">Lady Six Sky</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kawiil-chan-kinich">K'awiil Chan K'inich</a> the kingdom overreached and in 761 it was defeated; the capital was ringed with hastily built walls.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After 761 the royal family moved to the fortified twin capital of Aguateca, which was burnt and abandoned around 810. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petexbatun">Petexbatún</a> wars are a key example of the warfare that accompanied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/classic-maya-collapse">Classic Maya collapse</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dos-pilas.jpg" alt="Dos Pilas" width="320" height="502"><figcaption>Image: Joanbanjo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panell_19,_Dos_Pilas,_museu_Nacional_d%27Arqueologia_i_Etnologia,_Guatemala_(MUNAE).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>629 CE – 810 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dos Pilas</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>B'ajlaj Chan K'awiil, Itzamnaaj K'awiil, K'awiil Chan K'inich</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Maya religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Classic Maya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/guatemala">Guatemala</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Petexbatun kingdom, Aguateca</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=720&amp;focus=dos-pilas" aria-label="Dos Pilas on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2221 1567 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Dos Pilas lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2541 1823L2564 1794M2541 1823L2564 1762"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2564 1794h0M2564 1762h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2541 1823h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2541 1823h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=720&amp;focus=dos-pilas">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
